  "workPackageTitle": "Per-category schemas and typed models: weapons and the stat price formula, branches, utilities, relics, PowerUps, and option unlocks",
  "notes": [
    "Entries are added before implementation and are never renumbered (docs/technical/91 § Verification registry).",
    "Every summary states the route the check takes to its subject, and names the gap where the route has one. See the same note in tests/verification/DAT-002.json.",
    "This repository has no CI. Every gate below is a local ./build.sh run.",
    "Fixture IDs are paths beneath tests/MechaMiner.Content.Tests/Fixtures/categories/. Every invalid fixture asserts the one diagnostic code it is named for.",
    "VER-DAT-003-026 is the over-strict control for this package.",
    "VER-DAT-003-003 is the compensation for recipes that are no longer human-legible. Once a recipe holds resource IDs rather than letters, a mis-assigned pair is invisible to a reader; resolving each ID to its canonical letter and comparing the concatenation to the weapon's own ID suffix restores the check a human used to perform by eye.",
    "Cross-reference existence - that a named resource, weapon, branch, relic or unlock definition is actually present - is DAT-005's relational work. Entries here check ID grammar and intra-catalog cardinality only, and say so."
